163 - At the Cross
 / 
Key: Eb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 163
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[Eb]Alas, and did my Savior bleed? And did my Sovereign [Bb7/F]die?
[Eb]Would He devote [Bb]that [Eb]sacred head For someone such asI?
[Eb]At the cross, at the cross where Ifirst [Fm/Ab]saw the [Eb/Bb]light,
[Bb7]And the [Eb]burden of my heart rolled away,

Refrain:
[Eb]At the [Bb]cross, at the cross,
[Bb]where I [Bb7]first saw the light,
[Bb7]and the burden [Eb]of my heart [Ab]rolled away;
[Ab/C]it was there by [Eb]faith I received my sight,
[Eb]and [Fm/Ab]now [Ab]I am [Bb7]happy all the [Eb]day!

Verse 2:
[Eb]Was it for crimes that I [Ab]have [Eb/G]done,
[Eb]he [Bb]groaned [Eb]upon the tree?
[Eb]Amazing pity! [Fm/Ab]Grace unknown!
[Bb7]And [Eb]love beyond degree!

Verse 3:
[Eb]But drops of grief can ne'er [Ab]repay
[Eb]the [Bb]debt [Eb]of love I owe:
[Eb]Here, Lord, I give myself [Fm/Ab]away;
[Bb7]'tis [Eb]all that I can do!
